{"parentUuid":"264afec9-2962-4d8f-a10e-0240871cbfcb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6eea6654-fcb4-4632-84f7-ce54400831f5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018FSGvEBVZrYY9VzmBVbA8f","type":"tool_result","content":"=== README history ===\nabd0ec6 02-06-1405\nD\tREADME.md\n5455046 Create README.md\nA\tREADME.md\n\n=== docs/*.md sizes ===\n0 docs/assumptions.md\n0 docs/decisions.md\n0 docs/experiments.md\n0 docs/literature.md\n0 docs/open_questions.md\n0 docs/research_questions.md\n0 total\n\n=== empty dirs (no files) ===\nsrc: 0 files\ntests: 0 files\nexperiments: 0 files\nresults: 0 files\nnotes: 0 files\ntheses: 0 files","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4592321f-7669-4db6-95e6-3b3f99be1562","timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:50:33.668Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== README history ===\nabd0ec6 02-06-1405\nD\tREADME.md\n5455046 Create README.md\nA\tREADME.md\n\n=== docs/*.md sizes ===\n0 docs/assumptions.md\n0 docs/decisions.md\n0 docs/experiments.md\n0 docs/literature.md\n0 docs/open_questions.md\n0 docs/research_questions.md\n0 total\n\n=== empty dirs (no files) ===\nsrc: 0 files\ntests: 0 files\nexperiments: 0 files\nresults: 0 files\nnotes: 0 files\ntheses: 0 files","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"264afec9-2962-4d8f-a10e-0240871cbfcb","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"496fd09e-b027-463d-b7cc-139da8d276a2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6eea6654-fcb4-4632-84f7-ce54400831f5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019v1NabBEq9AtNCUFZDdMag","type":"tool_result","content":"=== last 6 lines + line count of each SKILL.md (completeness check) ===\n--- change-impact : 627 lines ---\nAbandoning the approved project whenever a new paper, idea, algorithm, or implementation opportunity appears.\n\nThe preferred path is:\n\n**detect the problem → verify it → determine impact → find the smallest scientifically valid correction → preserve the approved direction whenever possible → obtain approval for material changes → implement → validate → update experiments, documentation, and thesis claims.**\n\n--- methodology-review : 569 lines ---\n\"A new paper exists, so the whole project should change.\"\n\nThe correct behavior is:\n\n**Preserve the approved research direction, aggressively detect scientific problems, propose the smallest evidence-based correction that restores validity, and require explicit approval for major changes.**\n\n--- novelty-check : 563 lines ---\nBe rigorous, skeptical, current, and scope-aware.\n\nThe goal is not to make the project look novel.\n\nThe goal is to determine what the project can **honestly and defensibly claim as its contribution**.\n\n--- research-review : 635 lines ---\n\r\nNever silently rewrite the thesis.\r\nNever blindly repeat an error because it appears in an approved document.\r\nNever optimize for agreement.\r\nOptimize for scientific validity, traceability, reproducibility, and defensibility.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bff9101b-7210-4f82-97ab-b2304e632c70","timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:50:36.796Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== last 6 lines + line count of each SKILL.md (completeness check) ===\n--- change-impact : 627 lines ---\nAbandoning the approved project whenever a new paper, idea, algorithm, or implementation opportunity appears.\n\nThe preferred path is:\n\n**detect the problem → verify it → determine impact → find the smallest scientifically valid correction → preserve the approved direction whenever possible → obtain approval for material changes → implement → validate → update experiments, documentation, and thesis claims.**\n\n--- methodology-review : 569 lines ---\n\"A new paper exists, so the whole project should change.\"\n\nThe correct behavior is:\n\n**Preserve the approved research direction, aggressively detect scientific problems, propose the smallest evidence-based correction that restores validity, and require explicit approval for major changes.**\n\n--- novelty-check : 563 lines ---\nBe rigorous, skeptical, current, and scope-aware.\n\nThe goal is not to make the project look novel.\n\nThe goal is to determine what the project can **honestly and defensibly claim as its contribution**.\n\n--- research-review : 635 lines ---\n\r\nNever silently rewrite the thesis.\r\nNever blindly repeat an error because it appears in an approved document.\r\nNever optimize for agreement.\r\nOptimize for scientific validity, traceability, reproducibility, and defensibility.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"496fd09e-b027-463d-b7cc-139da8d276a2","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
