{"parentUuid":"39321e4d-402c-4da6-b0ec-3abf2e36b774","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}],"id":"804485b73f4a62cc436732190af94ba8","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5863,"cache_read_input_tokens":245202,"output_tokens":2488,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5863},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"2026082506133691706678784dbpz6Q8wUtw","type":"assistant","uuid":"d920c758-83af-455f-bcb7-be26eedeedc8","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:14:06.142Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d920c758-83af-455f-bcb7-be26eedeedc8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"**یافته بحرانی پنجم — مستقیماً علیه توجیه PPO در سمینار:** در Negm 2024، در هیچ‌یک از سه مطالعه موردی **PPO برنده نشد** — روی Jowitt & Xu بهترین **TQC**، روی شبکه واقعی SZ08 بهترین **TRPO**، و در سناریوی burst بهترین **A2C** (پاداش ۴۲.۱۵) بود.\n\nحالا جست‌وجوی ادبیات خارجی ۲۰۲۵–۲۰۲۶ را موازی با تأیید منابع محلی آغاز می‌کنم:","type":"text"}],"id":"804485b73f4a62cc436732190af94ba8","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5863,"cache_read_input_tokens":245202,"output_tokens":2488,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5863},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"2026082506133691706678784dbpz6Q8wUtw","type":"assistant","uuid":"d0539bf2-d4dc-4d48-8ad7-3937a747f2b5","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:14:12.077Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d0539bf2-d4dc-4d48-8ad7-3937a747f2b5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01KWuVnHJBQbbQGBhrhTXVNi","input":{"command":"F=\"papers/Real-Time Scheduling of Pumps in Water Distribution Systems Based on Exploration-Enhanced Deep Reinforcement Learning.pdf\"; pdftotext -f 1 -l 2 -enc UTF-8 \"$F\" - 2>/dev/null | head -c 2200","description":"Verify E-PPO paper abstract"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"804485b73f4a62cc436732190af94ba8","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5863,"cache_read_input_tokens":245202,"output_tokens":2488,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5863},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"2026082506133691706678784dbpz6Q8wUtw","type":"assistant","uuid":"ff71c271-1cd7-4e98-8b48-003356d8e795","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:14:13.515Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ff71c271-1cd7-4e98-8b48-003356d8e795","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_019AYRH9NzQJhfBNsm7zw3Pp","input":{"query":"deep reinforcement learning coordinated PRV and pump pressure management water distribution network 2025 2026"},"name":"WebSearch","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"804485b73f4a62cc436732190af94ba8","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5863,"cache_read_input_tokens":245202,"output_tokens":2488,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5863},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"2026082506133691706678784dbpz6Q8wUtw","type":"assistant","uuid":"3291550d-5ecd-457b-ad86-e6df9ca7dd00","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:14:13.949Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ff71c271-1cd7-4e98-8b48-003356d8e795","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ff3c19c5-aaaf-4dec-bdcc-1d127ee3c9f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KWuVnHJBQbbQGBhrhTXVNi","type":"tool_result","content":"systems\r\n\r\nArticle\r\nReal-Time Scheduling of Pumps in Water Distribution Systems Based on Exploration-Enhanced Deep Reinforcement Learning\r\nShiyuan Hu 1, Jinliang Gao 1,* , Dan Zhong 1, Rui Wu 2 and Luming Liu 3\r\n\r\n1 School of Environment, Harbin Institute of Technology, Harbin 150090, China 2 Guangdong Yuehai Water Investment Co., Ltd., Shenzhen 518021, China 3 National Engineering Research Center of Urban Water Resources Co., Ltd., Harbin Institute of Technology,\r\nHarbin 150090, China\r\n* Correspondence: gjl@hit.edu.cn\r\n\r\nAbstract: Effective ways to optimise real-time pump scheduling to maximise energy efﬁciency are being sought to meet the challenges in the energy market. However, the considerable number of evaluations of popular optimisation methods based on metaheuristics cause signiﬁcant delays for real-time pump scheduling, and the simpliﬁcation of traditional deterministic methods may introduce bias towards the optimal solutions. To address these limitations, an exploration-enhanced deep reinforcement learning (DRL) framework is proposed to address real-time pump scheduling problems in water distribution systems. The experimental results indicate that E-PPO can learn suboptimal scheduling policies for various demand distributions and can control the application time to 0.42 s by transferring the online computation-intensive optimisation task ofﬂine. Furthermore, a form of penalty of the tank level was found that can reduce energy costs by up to 11.14% without sacriﬁcing the water level in the long term. Following the DRL framework, the proposed method makes it possible to schedule pumps in a more agile way as a timely response to changing water demand while still controlling the energy cost and level of tanks.\r\n\r\nCitation: Hu, S.; Gao, J.; Zhong, D.; Wu, R.; Liu, L. Real-Time Scheduling of Pumps in Water Distribution Systems Based on Exploration-Enhanced Deep Reinforcement Learning. Systems 2023, 11, 56. https://doi.org/ 10.3390/systems11020056\r\nAcademic Editor: William T. Scherer\r\nReceived: 13 December 2022 Revised: 11 January 2023 Accepted: 18 January 2023 Published: 20 January 2023\r\nCopyright: © 2023 by the authors. Licensee MDPI, Basel, Swit","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"04f95125-a978-4cdb-a554-5a2d8109acc1","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:14:14.116Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"systems\r\n\r\nArticle\r\nReal-Time Scheduling of Pumps in Water Distribution Systems Based on Exploration-Enhanced Deep Reinforcement Learning\r\nShiyuan Hu 1, Jinliang Gao 1,* , Dan Zhong 1, Rui Wu 2 and Luming Liu 3\r\n\r\n1 School of Environment, Harbin Institute of Technology, Harbin 150090, China 2 Guangdong Yuehai Water Investment Co., Ltd., Shenzhen 518021, China 3 National Engineering Research Center of Urban Water Resources Co., Ltd., Harbin Institute of Technology,\r\nHarbin 150090, China\r\n* Correspondence: gjl@hit.edu.cn\r\n\r\nAbstract: Effective ways to optimise real-time pump scheduling to maximise energy efﬁciency are being sought to meet the challenges in the energy market. However, the considerable number of evaluations of popular optimisation methods based on metaheuristics cause signiﬁcant delays for real-time pump scheduling, and the simpliﬁcation of traditional deterministic methods may introduce bias towards the optimal solutions. To address these limitations, an exploration-enhanced deep reinforcement learning (DRL) framework is proposed to address real-time pump scheduling problems in water distribution systems. The experimental results indicate that E-PPO can learn suboptimal scheduling policies for various demand distributions and can control the application time to 0.42 s by transferring the online computation-intensive optimisation task ofﬂine. Furthermore, a form of penalty of the tank level was found that can reduce energy costs by up to 11.14% without sacriﬁcing the water level in the long term. Following the DRL framework, the proposed method makes it possible to schedule pumps in a more agile way as a timely response to changing water demand while still controlling the energy cost and level of tanks.\r\n\r\nCitation: Hu, S.; Gao, J.; Zhong, D.; Wu, R.; Liu, L. Real-Time Scheduling of Pumps in Water Distribution Systems Based on Exploration-Enhanced Deep Reinforcement Learning. Systems 2023, 11, 56. https://doi.org/ 10.3390/systems11020056\r\nAcademic Editor: William T. Scherer\r\nReceived: 13 December 2022 Revised: 11 January 2023 Accepted: 18 January 2023 Published: 20 January 2023\r\nCopyright: © 2023 by the authors. Licensee MDPI, Basel, Swit","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ff71c271-1cd7-4e98-8b48-003356d8e795","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
