{"parentUuid":"5484a602-1998-419f-a183-4c5e18885514","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6785fb76-59d2-4c04-ae7f-c3e6eb641817","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01GYDA6WJPSYRE8bAU3wz3R2","type":"tool_result","content":"=== NETWORK IDENTITY ===\nr ak values (Giustolisi et al. 2008). In the case study, a value of ak ¼ 1:2 was selected according to Giustolisi et al. (2013), Jowitt & Xu (1990) and Vairavamoorthy & Lumbers (1998). The parameter bk depends not only on the pipe characteristics but also on the as\n contrary to the concept of a multi-agent reward. Therefore, agents consider random interactions with the environment to obtain a benchmark cost. Then, this benchmark is subtracted by the cost generated at each time step to construct the reward. In addition, penalties \nntroducing the studied WDN EPANET Net 3 was trained and tested in this study. The EPANET Net 3 network is one of the most popular benchmarks for WDN optimisation tasks because of its data availability and ﬂexibility for modiﬁcation (Mala-Jetmarova et al. 2017). The\nresources in pressurized systems: competition at WDSA 2014. Journal of Water Resources Planning and Management 142 (5), C4015002. Jowitt, P. W. & Xu, C. 1990 Optimal valve control in water-distribution networks. Journal of Water Resources Planning and Management 116","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0e9a0ef8-b058-4a08-9378-28fd838d221f","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:46:57.250Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== NETWORK IDENTITY ===\nr ak values (Giustolisi et al. 2008). In the case study, a value of ak ¼ 1:2 was selected according to Giustolisi et al. (2013), Jowitt & Xu (1990) and Vairavamoorthy & Lumbers (1998). The parameter bk depends not only on the pipe characteristics but also on the as\n contrary to the concept of a multi-agent reward. Therefore, agents consider random interactions with the environment to obtain a benchmark cost. Then, this benchmark is subtracted by the cost generated at each time step to construct the reward. In addition, penalties \nntroducing the studied WDN EPANET Net 3 was trained and tested in this study. The EPANET Net 3 network is one of the most popular benchmarks for WDN optimisation tasks because of its data availability and ﬂexibility for modiﬁcation (Mala-Jetmarova et al. 2017). The\nresources in pressurized systems: competition at WDSA 2014. Journal of Water Resources Planning and Management 142 (5), C4015002. Jowitt, P. W. & Xu, C. 1990 Optimal valve control in water-distribution networks. Journal of Water Resources Planning and Management 116","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5484a602-1998-419f-a183-4c5e18885514","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
