{"parentUuid":"97d11a72-58c5-482c-8973-42efa2d806da","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01WmVHdkxj1qCK4q6q5XgNa3","input":{"command":"F=\"/d/Thesis/papers/Real-Time Scheduling of Pumps in Water Distribution Systems Based on Exploration-Enhanced Deep Reinforcement Learning.pdf\"; echo \"=== GA vs PPO — PRIMARY SOURCE ===\"; pdftotext -enc UTF-8 \"$F\" - 2>/dev/null | grep -aoiE \".{150}(GA (was|converged|obtained|achiev|outperf)|optimal solution|best solution|compared with (the )?(GA|metaheuristic)).{170}\" | head -6","description":"Verify GA vs PPO from primary source"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"c602b426ce2938e816f299bc8bd19156","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4825,"cache_read_input_tokens":333613,"output_tokens":3061,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4825},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"20260825064700428125442fcmflrkyTroQm","type":"assistant","uuid":"32a8778d-45a2-406e-aebc-f2012b6df20e","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:47:44.803Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"97d11a72-58c5-482c-8973-42efa2d806da","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6785fb76-59d2-4c04-ae7f-c3e6eb641817","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Dx74YPtpgKL2bsngvK25H7","type":"tool_result","content":"## Result 1\n\n**Title:** \"Deep reinforcement learning for integrated data assimilation and valve control in water distribution systems\"\n**Authors:** Minhyuk Jeung (first; ORCID 0000-0001-5074-5973), In-Su Jang, Hyun-Su Bae, Kwang-Ju Kim, Jung-Won Yu, Mi-Seon Kang, Younggu Her (ORCID 0000-0003-3700-5115), Seok Min Hong, Sang-Soo Baek — no affiliations listed\n**Container title:** \"Water Research X\"\n**Published:** May 2026\n**DOI:** 10.1016/j.wroa.2026.100540\n**Type:** journal-article\n**Abstract:** none in the record\n\n## Result 2\n\n**Title:** \"Data Assimilation in Chaotic Systems Using Deep Reinforcement Learning\"\n**Authors:** Mohamad Abed El Rahman Hammoud (first; KAUST; ORCID 0000-0003-1896-4927), Naila Raboudi (KAUST), Edriss S Titi (University of Cambridge), Omar M Knio (KAUST; ORCID 0000-0002-0973-1112), Ibrahim Hoteit (listed as \"King Abdullah Univerity of Science and Technology\"; ORCID 0000-0002-3751-4393)\n**Container title:** none\n**Published:** 27 December 2023\n**DOI:** 10.22541/essoar.170365205.56063528/v1\n**Type:** posted-content\n**Abstract (summarized — too long to quote in full):** The authors note that data assimilation matters for uses spanning climate and weather prediction through to route planning for self-driving vehicles, and that the ensemble Kalman filter (EnKF) depends on linear updates that reduce ensemble variance. They argue recent deep learning work has been largely supervised, leaving open the question of how well such models generalize to situations they were not trained on. Their proposal applies reinforcement learning to correct model states from complete or incomplete observations, tested on the chaotic Lorenz '63 system, where the agent aims \"to minimize the root-mean-squared error between the observations and corresponding forecast states.\" Because the action policy is stochastic, repeated sampling yields an ensemble of assimilated realizations in a Monte Carlo framework. Reported outcomes compare favorably with the EnKF, and the agent can also handle non-Gaussian data, which they describe as \"a significant limitation of the EnKF.\"\n\n## Result 3\n\n**Title:** \"Energy efficient online control of a water distribution network based on Deep Reinforcement Learning\"\n**Authors:** Baltasar Beferull-Lozano, Jyotirmoy Bhardwaj, Helge Liltvedt (all three tagged with sequence \"first\"; no affiliations)\n**Container title:** none\n**Published:** 14 August 2023\n**DOI:** 10.36227/techrxiv.23896902\n**Type:** posted-content\n**Abstract:** \"Data is obtained via Deep Reinforcement Learning Environment\"\n\n*Note: the response is a Crossref work list reporting 1,851,357 total results, with 3 items per page returned here.*"}]},"uuid":"242014fa-8fc5-4a03-be51-d85cfa7c219d","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:48:10.416Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":5438,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## Result 1\n\n**Title:** \"Deep reinforcement learning for integrated data assimilation and valve control in water distribution systems\"\n**Authors:** Minhyuk Jeung (first; ORCID 0000-0001-5074-5973), In-Su Jang, Hyun-Su Bae, Kwang-Ju Kim, Jung-Won Yu, Mi-Seon Kang, Younggu Her (ORCID 0000-0003-3700-5115), Seok Min Hong, Sang-Soo Baek — no affiliations listed\n**Container title:** \"Water Research X\"\n**Published:** May 2026\n**DOI:** 10.1016/j.wroa.2026.100540\n**Type:** journal-article\n**Abstract:** none in the record\n\n## Result 2\n\n**Title:** \"Data Assimilation in Chaotic Systems Using Deep Reinforcement Learning\"\n**Authors:** Mohamad Abed El Rahman Hammoud (first; KAUST; ORCID 0000-0003-1896-4927), Naila Raboudi (KAUST), Edriss S Titi (University of Cambridge), Omar M Knio (KAUST; ORCID 0000-0002-0973-1112), Ibrahim Hoteit (listed as \"King Abdullah Univerity of Science and Technology\"; ORCID 0000-0002-3751-4393)\n**Container title:** none\n**Published:** 27 December 2023\n**DOI:** 10.22541/essoar.170365205.56063528/v1\n**Type:** posted-content\n**Abstract (summarized — too long to quote in full):** The authors note that data assimilation matters for uses spanning climate and weather prediction through to route planning for self-driving vehicles, and that the ensemble Kalman filter (EnKF) depends on linear updates that reduce ensemble variance. They argue recent deep learning work has been largely supervised, leaving open the question of how well such models generalize to situations they were not trained on. Their proposal applies reinforcement learning to correct model states from complete or incomplete observations, tested on the chaotic Lorenz '63 system, where the agent aims \"to minimize the root-mean-squared error between the observations and corresponding forecast states.\" Because the action policy is stochastic, repeated sampling yields an ensemble of assimilated realizations in a Monte Carlo framework. Reported outcomes compare favorably with the EnKF, and the agent can also handle non-Gaussian data, which they describe as \"a significant limitation of the EnKF.\"\n\n## Result 3\n\n**Title:** \"Energy efficient online control of a water distribution network based on Deep Reinforcement Learning\"\n**Authors:** Baltasar Beferull-Lozano, Jyotirmoy Bhardwaj, Helge Liltvedt (all three tagged with sequence \"first\"; no affiliations)\n**Container title:** none\n**Published:** 14 August 2023\n**DOI:** 10.36227/techrxiv.23896902\n**Type:** posted-content\n**Abstract:** \"Data is obtained via Deep Reinforcement Learning Environment\"\n\n*Note: the response is a Crossref work list reporting 1,851,357 total results, with 3 items per page returned here.*","durationMs":28074,"url":"https://api.crossref.org/works?query.bibliographic=Deep+Reinforcement+Learning+Integrated+Data+Assimilation+Valve+Control+Water+Distribution+Systems&rows=3&select=title,author,container-title,published,DOI,abstract,type"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"97d11a72-58c5-482c-8973-42efa2d806da","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
