{"parentUuid":"70cf5259-c129-48d4-a140-8178168e9cc0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"**Jeung et al. 2026 — CONFIRMED:** «Deep reinforcement learning for integrated data assimilation and valve control in water distribution systems», **Water Research X**, می ۲۰۲۶, DOI **10.1016/j.wroa.2026.100540**, ۹ نویسنده (Minhyuk Jeung و همکاران).\n\n**⚠️ تصحیح مهم نسبت به Phase 1.5:** ادعای «GA از PPO بهتر بود» از **منبع ثانویه** (نقل Negm) است. جداول ۲ و ۳ مقاله اصلی استخراج نشدند. تلاش با `-layout`:","type":"text"}],"id":"9e0331f6dd78c70a33a65699db487556","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4582,"cache_read_input_tokens":338438,"output_tokens":1772,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4582},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"20260825064813574766186lbls8a9uuzRpz","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c1a9dc7-f169-498c-961c-e7ce29c1e895","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:48:37.292Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"9c1a9dc7-f169-498c-961c-e7ce29c1e895","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01Rnc2HNZQLDtzNiih6pUTc8","input":{"command":"F=\"/d/Thesis/papers/Real-Time Scheduling of Pumps in Water Distribution Systems Based on Exploration-Enhanced Deep Reinforcement Learning.pdf\"; echo \"=== TABLE 2/3 via -layout ===\"; pdftotext -layout -enc UTF-8 \"$F\" - 2>/dev/null | grep -a -A12 -iE \"Table 2\\.|Table 3\\.\" | head -50","description":"Extract Hu Systems Tables 2-3 with layout preservation"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"9e0331f6dd78c70a33a65699db487556","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4582,"cache_read_input_tokens":338438,"output_tokens":1772,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4582},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"20260825064813574766186lbls8a9uuzRpz","type":"assistant","uuid":"449b736e-ec6d-40c1-8d9d-b39816fa31de","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:48:39.188Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"449b736e-ec6d-40c1-8d9d-b39816fa31de","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6785fb76-59d2-4c04-ae7f-c3e6eb641817","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Rnc2HNZQLDtzNiih6pUTc8","type":"tool_result","content":"=== TABLE 2/3 via -layout ===\n                               Table 2. Comparison of E-PPO, PPO, and metaheuristics performance for the test cases.\n\nUncertainty                                                 Energy Cost (USD/Day)\nParameter of\n                      Test Case    GA               PSO                    DE       PPO         E-PPO\n  Demand\n      0.30              Case 1   190.251           231.889               205.586   213.210      207.941\n                        Case 2   193.700           256.125               231.793   215.387      209.001\n      0.60              Case 3   206.623           283.127               239.610   218.477      215.993\n                        Case 4   198.713           242.322               229.684   218.099      211.868\n      0.90              Case 5   190.328           223.991               212.200   237.575      215.848\n\n                        Case 1   194.435           279.038               223.849   214.965      206.268\n--\n                               Table 3. Computation time of the models.\n\nUncertainty             GA        PSO       DE              Time (s)      E-PPO         PPO        E-PPO\nParameter of                                                             Training  Application  Application\n                      1699.32    1291.18  1448.63             PPO\n  Demand              1640.72    1214.62  1475.45           Training      5573.58       0.42         0.41\n                      1586.19    1181.03  1408.05                         5407.01       0.44         0.42\n      0.3                                                    5479.30      5506.07       0.42         0.42\n      0.6                                                    5333.92\n      0.9                                                    5833.19\n\n                                     GA converges after 100 epochs of training; therefore, the results of GA are considered\n                               as optimal solutions and benchmarks for test cases in this paper. As shown in Table 2,\n--\n                                       in Table 3. This is an almost negligible time consumption for hourly scheduling. However,\n                                       the computation time of the GA is nearly half an hour, which is impractical for hourly\n                                       scheduling. The performance of the E-PPO is only slightly worse than that of GA, but the\n                                       application time cost of the E-PPO is only less than a second. As time is a very important\n                                       factor in industrial production, E-PPO is a potential real-time scheduling method to obtain\n                                       suboptimal solutions.\n\n                                       4. Conclusions\n\n                                              In this paper, the real-time scheduling of pumps in water distribution systems based on\n                                       exploration-enhanced deep reinforcement learning is proposed. By constructing a reward\n                                       function, the penalty form of the tank level was explored. We found a form that can make\n                                       full use of the storage and regulation capacity of the tanks that also saves up to 11.14%","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2f6e8187-498e-4513-bf49-bafdf270fd60","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:48:39.599Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== TABLE 2/3 via -layout ===\n                               Table 2. Comparison of E-PPO, PPO, and metaheuristics performance for the test cases.\n\nUncertainty                                                 Energy Cost (USD/Day)\nParameter of\n                      Test Case    GA               PSO                    DE       PPO         E-PPO\n  Demand\n      0.30              Case 1   190.251           231.889               205.586   213.210      207.941\n                        Case 2   193.700           256.125               231.793   215.387      209.001\n      0.60              Case 3   206.623           283.127               239.610   218.477      215.993\n                        Case 4   198.713           242.322               229.684   218.099      211.868\n      0.90              Case 5   190.328           223.991               212.200   237.575      215.848\n\n                        Case 1   194.435           279.038               223.849   214.965      206.268\n--\n                               Table 3. Computation time of the models.\n\nUncertainty             GA        PSO       DE              Time (s)      E-PPO         PPO        E-PPO\nParameter of                                                             Training  Application  Application\n                      1699.32    1291.18  1448.63             PPO\n  Demand              1640.72    1214.62  1475.45           Training      5573.58       0.42         0.41\n                      1586.19    1181.03  1408.05                         5407.01       0.44         0.42\n      0.3                                                    5479.30      5506.07       0.42         0.42\n      0.6                                                    5333.92\n      0.9                                                    5833.19\n\n                                     GA converges after 100 epochs of training; therefore, the results of GA are considered\n                               as optimal solutions and benchmarks for test cases in this paper. As shown in Table 2,\n--\n                                       in Table 3. This is an almost negligible time consumption for hourly scheduling. However,\n                                       the computation time of the GA is nearly half an hour, which is impractical for hourly\n                                       scheduling. The performance of the E-PPO is only slightly worse than that of GA, but the\n                                       application time cost of the E-PPO is only less than a second. As time is a very important\n                                       factor in industrial production, E-PPO is a potential real-time scheduling method to obtain\n                                       suboptimal solutions.\n\n                                       4. Conclusions\n\n                                              In this paper, the real-time scheduling of pumps in water distribution systems based on\n                                       exploration-enhanced deep reinforcement learning is proposed. By constructing a reward\n                                       function, the penalty form of the tank level was explored. We found a form that can make\n                                       full use of the storage and regulation capacity of the tanks that also saves up to 11.14%","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"449b736e-ec6d-40c1-8d9d-b39816fa31de","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
