{"parentUuid":"7848fe96-2ecd-4f6c-b7a6-373a6976322c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"**تأیید کامل از منبع اصلی — `-layout` جواب داد.** جدول ۲ و ۳ مقاله Hu et al. (Systems 11(2):56):\n\n| عدم‌قطعیت | Case | **GA** | PSO | DE | PPO | E-PPO |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.30 | 1 | **190.25** | 231.89 | 205.59 | 213.21 | 207.94 |\n| 0.30 | 2 | **193.70** | 256.13 | 231.79 | 215.39 | 209.00 |\n| 0.60 | 3 | **206.62** | 283.13 | 239.61 | 218.48 | 215.99 |\n| 0.60 | 4 | **198.71** | 242.32 | 229.68 | 218.10 | 211.87 |\n| **0.90** | 5 | **190.33** | 223.99 | 212.20 | **237.58** ⚠️ | 215.85 |\n\nنقل مستقیم: «**GA converges after 100 epochs… therefore, the results of GA are considered as optimal solutions and benchmarks**» و «GA… nearly **half an hour**… E-PPO… **less than a second**… **suboptimal solutions**».\n\n**یافته جدید بحرانی:** در بالاترین سطح عدم‌قطعیت (۰.۹)، **PPO خالص بدترین عملکرد را دارد (۲۳۷.۵۸)** — دقیقاً رژیمی که سؤال فرعی ۱ پروژه شما هدف گرفته.\n\nتأیید ادعای PDA در Hu MARL (که در Phase 1.5 گفتم):","type":"text"}],"id":"32af70408a4a7651c9a84b43f8d58584","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2723,"cache_read_input_tokens":343020,"output_tokens":2327,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2723},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"20260825064844447580634g7cmjp8JSbKxE","type":"assistant","uuid":"be2396d8-72f6-49a1-9877-389312e722cb","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:49:15.465Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"be2396d8-72f6-49a1-9877-389312e722cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01EqfNkdpkCGngejKBGxazJr","input":{"command":"F=\"/d/Thesis/papers/Multi-agent reinforcement learning framework for real-time scheduling of pump and valve in water distribution networks.pdf\"; echo \"=== what are the 'PDA' hits? ===\"; pdftotext -enc UTF-8 \"$F\" - 2>/dev/null | grep -aoiE \".{45}PDA.{45}\" | head -8; echo; echo \"=== demand model / leakage formulation ===\"; pdftotext -enc UTF-8 \"$F\" - 2>/dev/null | grep -aoiE \".{100}(background leakage|leakage (model|is calculated|exponent)|demand-driven|pressure-driven).{130}\" | head -5","description":"Verify PDA claim in Hu MARL paper"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"32af70408a4a7651c9a84b43f8d58584","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2723,"cache_read_input_tokens":343020,"output_tokens":2327,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2723},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"20260825064844447580634g7cmjp8JSbKxE","type":"assistant","uuid":"e16bdc30-eb6a-4410-b75d-2b93cd0e1a68","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:49:20.019Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e16bdc30-eb6a-4410-b75d-2b93cd0e1a68","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6785fb76-59d2-4c04-ae7f-c3e6eb641817","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01EqfNkdpkCGngejKBGxazJr","type":"tool_result","content":"=== what are the 'PDA' hits? ===\nmeters of target networks umQ0 and umm0 are updated based on the parameters of evaluated netw\n\n=== demand model / leakage formulation ===\n operation of the pump and valve can reduce energy consumption and water loss. However, the cost of background leakage conﬂicts with the energy cost of pumps (Giustolisi et al. 2013). During night-time, more water is pumped to supplement tank sto\neakage demand signiﬁcantly varies with changes in pressure. Giustolisi et al. (2008) computed the background leakage at the pipe level based on the average pressure of the pipe. This method was simulated using a pressuredriven strategy instead of\npressure of the end nodes. Giustolisi et al. (2016) pointed out that, except for the case where the leakage exponent is 1, this simpliﬁcation will cause errors in evaluating the leakages. Eck et al. (2014) developed a technique using the emitte\n including background leakage, is essential for evaluating the water loss element of the objective. Background leakage is caused by small outﬂows from cracks and ﬁttings. Germanopoulos (1985) proposed a model to compute background leakages at t\n J., Arandia, E., Naoum-Sawaya, J. & Wirth, F. 2014 A simulation-optimization approach for reducing background leakage in water systems. Procedia Engineering 89, 59–68. Gao, J., Qi, S., Wu, W., Han, A., Chen, C. & Ruan, T. 2014 Leakage control of","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"da5ca2ce-9e31-45f1-a3e4-88e7a303d418","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:49:24.236Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== what are the 'PDA' hits? ===\nmeters of target networks umQ0 and umm0 are updated based on the parameters of evaluated netw\n\n=== demand model / leakage formulation ===\n operation of the pump and valve can reduce energy consumption and water loss. However, the cost of background leakage conﬂicts with the energy cost of pumps (Giustolisi et al. 2013). During night-time, more water is pumped to supplement tank sto\neakage demand signiﬁcantly varies with changes in pressure. Giustolisi et al. (2008) computed the background leakage at the pipe level based on the average pressure of the pipe. This method was simulated using a pressuredriven strategy instead of\npressure of the end nodes. Giustolisi et al. (2016) pointed out that, except for the case where the leakage exponent is 1, this simpliﬁcation will cause errors in evaluating the leakages. Eck et al. (2014) developed a technique using the emitte\n including background leakage, is essential for evaluating the water loss element of the objective. Background leakage is caused by small outﬂows from cracks and ﬁttings. Germanopoulos (1985) proposed a model to compute background leakages at t\n J., Arandia, E., Naoum-Sawaya, J. & Wirth, F. 2014 A simulation-optimization approach for reducing background leakage in water systems. Procedia Engineering 89, 59–68. Gao, J., Qi, S., Wu, W., Han, A., Chen, C. & Ruan, T. 2014 Leakage control of","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e16bdc30-eb6a-4410-b75d-2b93cd0e1a68","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
