{"parentUuid":"0665084c-441f-4e64-be0d-7a7199555ec7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"**اصلاح دقیق:** اپیزود = **۲۴ گام (یک روز، ساعتی)**، پس ۲۰,۰۰۰ گام ≈ **۸۳۳ اپیزود** — که برای PPO روی کنترل پیوسته چند-PRV هنوز بسیار کم است (شاید ~۱۰ به‌روزرسانی سیاست).\n\nجداول ۵-۴ و ۵-۵ ناقص استخراج شدند. تلاش هدفمند روی صفحات:","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_bdrk_sgie6nnaccmle3kemy4fx36qgycmy3raj5zesbedzhw4clqbhsca","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362323,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1678,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":362323},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"20260825065638731515433fcmflWEH0KmfX","type":"assistant","uuid":"103cd387-7fec-4247-884d-9622481b3c5e","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:57:08.294Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"103cd387-7fec-4247-884d-9622481b3c5e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_013G6o4RKnyMHUCxz5ihtnEn","input":{"command":"F=\"/d/Thesis/papers/Water pressure optimisation for leakage management using deep reinforcement learning.pdf\"; pdftotext -layout -f 147 -l 149 -enc UTF-8 \"$F\" - 2>/dev/null | head -45","description":"Extract Negm Table 5-4 page directly"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"id":"msg_bdrk_sgie6nnaccmle3kemy4fx36qgycmy3raj5zesbedzhw4clqbhsca","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362323,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1678,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":362323},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"20260825065638731515433fcmflWEH0KmfX","type":"assistant","uuid":"f5e8a514-76ea-453f-84e2-0439f303bb67","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:57:09.589Z","effort":"max","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f5e8a514-76ea-453f-84e2-0439f303bb67","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6785fb76-59d2-4c04-ae7f-c3e6eb641817","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013G6o4RKnyMHUCxz5ihtnEn","type":"tool_result","content":"            Training Times  Processing time of different algorithms in seconds\r\n\r\nAlgorithms                                                                                                                               SAC\r\n                                                                                                                                         Tuned\r\n            Test Times                                                                                                                   ARS\r\n                                                                                                                                         Tuned\r\n                                                                                                                                         TQC\r\n                                                                                                                                         Tuned\r\n                                                                                                                                         ARS\r\n\r\n                                                                                                                                         TQC\r\n\r\n                                                                                                                                         SAC\r\n\r\n                                                                                                                                         DE\r\n\r\n                                                                                                                                         PSO\r\n\r\n                                                                                                                                         NM\r\n\r\n            0               200 400 600 800 1000 1200 1400 1600 1800 2000\r\n                            Time in seconds\r\n\r\n                            Figure 5-7 Tuned algorithm speed - Jowitt & Xu network.\r\n\r\nMoreover, the key episodic results of the case study are displayed below in table 5-4. The\r\nalgorithms’ performances in maximising rewards, maximising water saved from leakage,\r\nminimising pressure violations, maximising carbon emission reductions and processing time.\r\nThe carbon emissions are calculated using water leakage measurements and the conversion\r\nfactor (176.7 KgCO2/million litres) dictated by the UK’s government values for the transport\r\nand distribution for 2023 presented in (Department for Energy Security and Net Zero, 2023).\r\nThe best result in each category is marked in bold. PPO and Recurrent PPO models yielded the\r\nhighest % of water saved at 73.4% and the highest carbon emissions reduction with 302.5\r\nkgCO2 reduced. However, this came at the expense of pressure violations that accumulated to\r\nthe values of 300 for Recurrent PPO and 304 for PPO. In contrast, DE showed the best pressure\r\nviolations minimisation with 46 violations and the best average episodic reward 995.2. Finally,\r\nthe best processing speed was achieved by PPO for training time and DDPG for test time.\r\nTable 5-4 shows how deploying the optimisation algorithms can lead to significant reductions\r\nin leakage and pressure violations. We discuss these results further and draw conclusions in\r\nthe next section.\r\n\r\n                            130\r\n\fTable 5-4 Key results – Jowitt & Xu\r\n\r\nAlgorithm  Average  Average          Average     Carbon     Training  Test","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"03ac8e51-5fac-4652-8604-ff7fc2351d84","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:57:09.844Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"            Training Times  Processing time of different algorithms in seconds\r\n\r\nAlgorithms                                                                                                                               SAC\r\n                                                                                                                                         Tuned\r\n            Test Times                                                                                                                   ARS\r\n                                                                                                                                         Tuned\r\n                                                                                                                                         TQC\r\n                                                                                                                                         Tuned\r\n                                                                                                                                         ARS\r\n\r\n                                                                                                                                         TQC\r\n\r\n                                                                                                                                         SAC\r\n\r\n                                                                                                                                         DE\r\n\r\n                                                                                                                                         PSO\r\n\r\n                                                                                                                                         NM\r\n\r\n            0               200 400 600 800 1000 1200 1400 1600 1800 2000\r\n                            Time in seconds\r\n\r\n                            Figure 5-7 Tuned algorithm speed - Jowitt & Xu network.\r\n\r\nMoreover, the key episodic results of the case study are displayed below in table 5-4. The\r\nalgorithms’ performances in maximising rewards, maximising water saved from leakage,\r\nminimising pressure violations, maximising carbon emission reductions and processing time.\r\nThe carbon emissions are calculated using water leakage measurements and the conversion\r\nfactor (176.7 KgCO2/million litres) dictated by the UK’s government values for the transport\r\nand distribution for 2023 presented in (Department for Energy Security and Net Zero, 2023).\r\nThe best result in each category is marked in bold. PPO and Recurrent PPO models yielded the\r\nhighest % of water saved at 73.4% and the highest carbon emissions reduction with 302.5\r\nkgCO2 reduced. However, this came at the expense of pressure violations that accumulated to\r\nthe values of 300 for Recurrent PPO and 304 for PPO. In contrast, DE showed the best pressure\r\nviolations minimisation with 46 violations and the best average episodic reward 995.2. Finally,\r\nthe best processing speed was achieved by PPO for training time and DDPG for test time.\r\nTable 5-4 shows how deploying the optimisation algorithms can lead to significant reductions\r\nin leakage and pressure violations. We discuss these results further and draw conclusions in\r\nthe next section.\r\n\r\n                            130\r\n\fTable 5-4 Key results – Jowitt & Xu\r\n\r\nAlgorithm  Average  Average          Average     Carbon     Training  Test","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f5e8a514-76ea-453f-84e2-0439f303bb67","session_id":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\Thesis","sessionId":"a4cbf1ac-8d99-42b4-9b8e-e55353a1e1c4","version":"2.1.240","gitBranch":"main"}
